    'cloud-devops-engineer',
    'Cloud and DevOps Engineer',
    'Cloud Computing',
    'Cloud and DevOps Engineers keep modern applications fast, reliable, secure and scalable.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Cloud and DevOps Engineer do?</h2><p>A Cloud and DevOps Engineer builds deployment pipelines, manages cloud infrastructure, improves reliability and supports engineering teams. This career is popular because startups, banks, SaaS companies and enterprise teams now run critical products on cloud platforms.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who enjoy systems, automation, debugging and reliability. <a href="/courses/btech">B.Tech</a>, <a href="/courses/bca">BCA</a> and <a href="/courses/mca">MCA</a> are practical routes.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn Linux, networking, Git, Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, monitoring, cloud basics and infrastructure as code. Real deployment projects matter more than certificates alone.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Roles are available in product engineering, IT services, platform teams, fintech and ecommerce. Freshers can start with cloud support, DevOps trainee or site reliability associate roles.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is DevOps only for experienced developers?</h3><p>No, but beginners need strong Linux, scripting and deployment practice.</p><h3>Which cloud should I learn?</h3><p>Any one major platform is fine at first. The concepts transfer across providers.</p>$career$,
