    'Full Stack Developer',
    'Software Development',
    'Full Stack Developers build complete web and app products across frontend, backend and databases.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Full Stack Developer do?</h2><p>A Full Stack Developer builds user interfaces, backend APIs, databases and integrations. It remains one of the most practical career paths because every business needs usable digital products, internal tools and customer-facing platforms.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This career suits students who like building visible products and learning by shipping. Strong routes include <a href="/courses/btech">B.Tech</a>, <a href="/courses/bca">BCA</a>, <a href="/courses/mca">MCA</a> and self-driven project learning.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, Node.js, databases, APIs, authentication and deployment. A portfolio with 3 to 5 working projects can matter more than a long certificate list.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Hiring exists in startups, agencies, SaaS, ecommerce, edtech, fintech and IT services. Entry roles include frontend developer, backend developer and junior full stack developer.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Can I become a developer without a CSE degree?</h3><p>Yes, if your projects, problem-solving and coding discipline are strong.</p><h3>What should I build first?</h3><p>Build a complete app with login, database, search, admin panel and deployment.</p>$career$,
