  (
    'ui-ux-designer',
    'UI UX Designer',
    'Design',
    'UI UX Designers create digital experiences that are useful, clear and easy to use.',
    $career$<h2>What does a UI UX Designer do?</h2><p>A UI UX Designer researches users, maps journeys, creates wireframes, designs interfaces and tests usability. The career is popular because every app, website and AI product needs a clean experience that real people can understand.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This role suits students who enjoy design, psychology, storytelling and problem solving. Relevant paths include <a href="/courses/bdes">B.Des</a>, design diplomas, <a href="/courses/btech">B.Tech</a> with product interest and self-built portfolios.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn user research, information architecture, Figma, visual hierarchy, prototyping, accessibility and design systems. A portfolio should explain the problem and decision process, not only show screens.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Demand is strong in product companies, design studios, fintech, ecommerce, SaaS and edtech. Entry roles include UI designer, UX researcher, product designer intern and interaction designer.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is drawing compulsory?</h3><p>No. Clear thinking, user empathy and interface judgment matter more than hand drawing.</p><h3>What should my portfolio include?</h3><p>Show research, problem framing, wireframes, final screens and what changed after feedback.</p>$career$,
