  (
    'digital-marketing-manager',
    'Digital Marketing Manager',
    'Marketing',
    'Digital Marketing Managers grow brands through search, content, social, paid campaigns and analytics.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Digital Marketing Manager do?</h2><p>A Digital Marketing Manager plans and improves campaigns across SEO, content, social media, paid ads, email and analytics. The career is popular because every college, startup, brand and local business needs measurable online growth.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This role suits students who enjoy creativity, numbers, writing and consumer behaviour. Useful routes include <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, commerce, mass communication and self-driven campaign projects.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn SEO, content planning, performance marketing, Google Analytics, social strategy, copywriting, landing pages and conversion tracking. Real campaign results are the best proof.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Hiring exists in agencies, ecommerce, edtech, D2C brands, SaaS, media and startups. Entry roles include SEO executive, content marketer, performance marketing associate and growth marketer.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is digital marketing only social media?</h3><p>No. It includes search, ads, email, analytics, content, conversion and retention.</p><h3>Can freshers start quickly?</h3><p>Yes, if they can show writing, analytics and campaign practice.</p>$career$,
