    'investment-banking-analyst',
    'Investment Banking Analyst',
    'Finance',
    'Investment Banking Analysts support deals, valuations, financial models and capital market transactions.',
    $career$<h2>What does an Investment Banking Analyst do?</h2><p>An Investment Banking Analyst builds financial models, researches companies, prepares pitch books and supports mergers, acquisitions, fundraising and market transactions. It is a competitive career because the work is analytical, high-pressure and closely linked to business decisions.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students with strong finance, Excel, accounting, valuation and communication skills. Common routes include <a href="/courses/bcom">B.Com</a>, <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, CA and economics.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn financial statements, valuation, Excel modelling, PowerPoint, market research and business writing. Internships and deal-style case studies are important.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Opportunities exist in investment banks, boutique advisory firms, private equity support, consulting and corporate finance teams. Entry roles are selective and usually require sharp preparation.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is MBA compulsory?</h3><p>No, but MBA, CA, economics or strong finance internships can improve access.</p><h3>Is the work intense?</h3><p>Yes. The role often has demanding hours, strict deadlines and high attention to detail.</p>$career$,
