    'FinTech Analyst',
    'FinTech',
    'FinTech Analysts work at the intersection of finance, technology, payments, lending and risk.',
    $career$<h2>What does a FinTech Analyst do?</h2><p>A FinTech Analyst studies digital payments, lending, credit risk, user behaviour, compliance and product performance. This career is growing because India has a large digital payments ecosystem and fast-moving financial technology companies.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who like finance, analytics, products and technology. Helpful courses include <a href="/courses/bcom">B.Com</a>, <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, <a href="/courses/btech">B.Tech</a> and analytics programmes.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Build SQL, Excel, product analytics, payments basics, credit risk, compliance awareness and dashboarding. Understanding RBI-led digital finance context is useful.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Roles exist in payments, lending, wealth-tech, insure-tech, banking product teams and risk analytics. Entry paths include product analyst, risk analyst, credit analyst and business analyst.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is FinTech only for engineers?</h3><p>No. Commerce, finance, management and analytics students can do well with technical literacy.</p><h3>What should I learn first?</h3><p>Start with finance basics, SQL, Excel and one payments or lending case study.</p>$career$,
