    'business-analyst',
    'Business Analyst',
    'Business Analytics',
    'Business Analysts convert business problems into requirements, insights and action plans.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Business Analyst do?</h2><p>A Business Analyst understands stakeholder needs, studies processes, analyses data and helps teams make better decisions. It is a popular career because it connects business, technology, operations and analytics without requiring deep coding from day one.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who like communication, logic, Excel, dashboards and structured problem solving. Useful routes include <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/bcom">B.Com</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, <a href="/courses/btech">B.Tech</a> and analytics courses.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn Excel, SQL basics, requirement writing, process mapping, Power BI, stakeholder communication and problem framing. Case studies are very useful for interviews.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Business analysts are hired in IT services, consulting, SaaS, banking, ecommerce, healthcare and operations teams. It is one of the easiest bridges from college to business-tech roles.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is business analyst a technical role?</h3><p>It can be semi-technical. SQL, dashboards and system understanding help a lot.</p><h3>Can freshers become business analysts?</h3><p>Yes. Freshers should show analytical projects, clear writing and strong communication.</p>$career$,
