    'Sustainability and ESG Specialist',
    'Sustainability',
    'Sustainability and ESG Specialists help organisations measure, report and improve environmental and social impact.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Sustainability and ESG Specialist do?</h2><p>A Sustainability and ESG Specialist works on climate reporting, carbon accounting, responsible sourcing, ESG disclosures and sustainability programmes. The career is growing as companies, investors and regulators pay closer attention to measurable impact.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who care about environment, policy, business and data. Helpful routes include <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, economics, environmental science, engineering and public policy.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn ESG frameworks, carbon accounting basics, Excel, data reporting, stakeholder communication, sustainability strategy and policy reading. Strong writing is important.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Opportunities exist in consulting, manufacturing, finance, real estate, energy, consumer goods and impact organisations. Entry roles include ESG analyst, sustainability analyst and climate reporting associate.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is ESG only for environmental science students?</h3><p>No. Business, finance, engineering and policy students can also enter this field.</p><h3>What makes a candidate strong?</h3><p>Data discipline, policy awareness, clear writing and practical project experience.</p>$career$,
