    'Healthcare Administrator',
    'Healthcare Management',
    'Healthcare Administrators manage hospital operations, patient services, teams, quality and compliance.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Healthcare Administrator do?</h2><p>A Healthcare Administrator manages hospital operations, patient flow, quality processes, billing coordination, compliance and service improvement. The career is popular because healthcare needs trained managers, not only doctors and nurses.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who like healthcare, operations, people management and systems. Helpful routes include <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, hospital administration, public health and allied health programmes.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn hospital operations, healthcare quality, Excel, communication, patient experience, compliance basics and team coordination. Internships in hospitals are highly valuable.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Roles exist in hospitals, clinics, health-tech companies, insurance operations and diagnostic chains. Entry roles include operations executive, patient services coordinator and hospital administration trainee.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Do I need an MBBS?</h3><p>No. Healthcare administration is a management path, though medical knowledge helps.</p><h3>Is this career only in hospitals?</h3><p>No. It also exists in health-tech, diagnostics, insurance and public health operations.</p>$career$,
