    'Clinical Research Associate',
    'Life Sciences',
    'Clinical Research Associates support trials, documentation and compliance for medicines and healthcare products.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Clinical Research Associate do?</h2><p>A Clinical Research Associate supports clinical trials by monitoring sites, checking documentation, coordinating with investigators and ensuring protocol compliance. The career matters because healthcare innovation needs safe, ethical and well-documented research.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students from pharmacy, life sciences, medicine, nursing and biotechnology who like detail, documentation and healthcare research. Useful routes include <a href="/courses/mbbs">MBBS</a>, pharmacy, biotechnology and life science courses.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn clinical trial basics, GCP, documentation, ethics, pharmacology basics, communication and Excel. Attention to detail is non-negotiable.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Roles exist in CROs, pharma companies, hospitals, biotech firms and medical device organisations. Entry roles include clinical trial coordinator, research associate and CRA trainee.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is this a lab-only career?</h3><p>No. It includes documentation, site monitoring, coordination and compliance work.</p><h3>Who can enter?</h3><p>Students from life sciences, pharmacy, nursing, medicine and allied health backgrounds are common fits.</p>$career$,
