    'Robotics Engineer',
    'Robotics and Automation',
    'Robotics Engineers design intelligent machines, automation systems and mechatronic products.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Robotics Engineer do?</h2><p>A Robotics Engineer works on mechanical design, electronics, sensors, control systems, software and automation. The career is gaining popularity because manufacturing, logistics, healthcare, defence and agriculture are using more automation.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who like machines, coding, electronics and building physical systems. Strong routes include <a href="/courses/btech">B.Tech</a> in mechanical, electronics, computer science, mechatronics or related engineering.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn C/C++, Python, control systems, embedded systems, CAD, sensors, ROS basics and electronics. Practical prototypes matter more than theory alone.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Roles exist in automation companies, manufacturing, drones, robotics startups, industrial IoT and research labs. Entry roles include robotics trainee, automation engineer and embedded systems engineer.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is robotics only mechanical engineering?</h3><p>No. Robotics blends mechanical, electronics, computer science and control systems.</p><h3>What project should I build?</h3><p>Start with a line follower, robotic arm, drone subsystem or sensor-based automation project.</p>$career$,
