    'Supply Chain Analyst',
    'Operations and Logistics',
    'Supply Chain Analysts improve inventory, logistics, planning, fulfilment and operational decisions.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Supply Chain Analyst do?</h2><p>A Supply Chain Analyst studies demand, inventory, transport, warehouse performance and fulfilment data. The career is important because ecommerce, manufacturing, retail and quick commerce need faster, smarter and more reliable operations.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who like operations, data, process improvement and practical business problems. Useful routes include <a href="/courses/bba">BBA</a>, <a href="/courses/mba">MBA</a>, engineering and commerce.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn Excel, SQL, forecasting, inventory basics, logistics metrics, Power BI and process mapping. Understanding real supply chain constraints is a big advantage.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Hiring exists in ecommerce, FMCG, manufacturing, logistics, retail and consulting. Entry roles include operations analyst, inventory analyst, logistics analyst and planning analyst.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Is this a desk job or field job?</h3><p>It can be both. Analysts often use data but must understand ground operations.</p><h3>Is MBA useful?</h3><p>Yes, especially for operations, supply chain and consulting roles.</p>$career$,
