    'Mental Health',
    'Psychologists and Counsellors support mental health, behaviour, learning and emotional wellbeing.',
    $career$<h2>What does a Psychologist and Counsellor do?</h2><p>A Psychologist or Counsellor helps people understand behaviour, emotions, stress, learning difficulties and life decisions. The career is gaining visibility as schools, colleges, workplaces and families take mental health more seriously.</p><h2>Best-fit students</h2><p>This path suits students who are patient, ethical, observant and good listeners. Useful routes include psychology, counselling, <a href="/courses/bachelor-of-science-bsc">B.Sc</a>, <a href="/courses/ma">MA</a> and postgraduate specialisations.</p><h2>Skills to build first</h2><p>Learn psychological foundations, counselling ethics, assessment basics, communication, case documentation and referral boundaries. Supervised training is essential.</p><h2>Career outlook</h2><p>Roles exist in schools, colleges, hospitals, clinics, NGOs, corporate wellbeing and private practice after the required qualifications. Always check licensing and practice rules for the chosen specialisation.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Can I practise after graduation?</h3><p>Independent practice usually needs higher study, supervised training and compliance with applicable rules.</p><h3>Is this career emotionally demanding?</h3><p>Yes. Self-care, supervision and ethical boundaries are important.</p>$career$,
